OL,3,GNEWSAPatient safety should be first -
OL,4,Asurgeons speak out on emergency general
OL,5,Asurgery
OL,6,
OL,7,FA leading surgeon in Northern Ireland
OL,8,Fhas said colleagues from across the UK
OL,9,Fand Ireland felt they had no option but
OL,10,Fto intervene when it appeared politics
OL,11,Fnot patient safety was influencing
OL,12,Fdiscussions on the provision of
OL,13,Femergency general surgery (EGS).
OL,15,FThe surgeons issued a statement after
OL,16,FHealth Minister Mike Nesbitt resigned
OL,17,Ffollowing a fall out with Ulster
OL,18,FUnionist Party (UUP) leader Jon Burrows
OL,19,Fover withdrawing EGS from Causeway
OL,20,FHospital.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,415,410,260,120,0,100
